abstract = {Inverters are the key to connecting the grid to new energy systems. Microgrid units controlled using a virtual synchronous generator (VSG) can switch between grid-connected and island modes for increased flexibility and reliability. When the big grid fails, the microgrid must be quickly disconnected and independently stabilized. In this paper, the risk measurement method and island detection technology are proposed to ensure the safety of microgrid units. To achieve seamless transitions from island mode to grid-connected mode, a precise model predictive control (MPC) strategy is implemented to enhance stability during the switching process. Ultimately, experiments are conducted under various scenarios to validate the effectiveness of the presented control strategy.},
